    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xCslDMbUHYI6"
      },
      "source": [
        "## A3C Questions [$10 \\times 3 = 30$ marks]\n",
        "\n",
        "### Q1. Why does A3C use asynchronous updates, and what benefit does this provide over synchronous (A2C) updates?\n",
        "Asynchronous updates basically allows multiple seeds of environment run at the same time parallely. Which will help the generalization capability of agent. If there are 8 agents then we can run 8 seeds of same environment the same time.\n",
        "\n",
        "Asynchronous updates allow the gradient to be updated as soon as a worker completes and episode instead of waiting for each of them to finish. Makes the algorithm faster.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Q2. What is the \"stale gradient\" problem in A3C and how does it affect learning?\n",
        "When a worker computes gradients and pushes them to the global network, other workers have already updated it in the meantime, so the gradients no longer match the current network weights. This mismatch slows down learning and can destabilize training since updates are based on an outdated policy.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Q3. Compare A3C with DQN in terms of memory requirements and training paradigm.\n",
        "DQN needs a large replay buffer in memory and learns off-policy from stored past experience on a single thread. A3C runs multiple workers in parallel, each discarding experience after use, so it needs far less memory and learns from fresh on-policy data.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "NLPHsEphaiYj"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Advantange Actor-Critic (A2C) [50 marks]\n",
        "<a id=\"a2c\"></a>\n",
        "\n",
        "A2C is the synchronous, deterministic variant of A3C. Instead of using asynchronous workers, A2C waits for all parallel workers to finish their rollouts before performing a single gradient update. This makes it simpler to implement and often equally effective.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Key ideas:**\n",
        "- Uses an Actor-Critic architecture: the actor outputs a policy $\\pi(a|s)$ and the critic estimates $V(s)$.\n",
        "- The advantage $A(s,a) = R_t - V(s_t)$ (or using GAE) is used to reduce variance in the policy gradient.\n",
        "- Multiple environments run in parallel (vectorized) and all updates are synchronous.\n",
        "- The loss combines: policy gradient loss, value loss, and an entropy bonus for exploration.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Policy Gradient with Advantage:**\n",
        "$$\\nabla_\\theta J(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}\\left[\\nabla_\\theta \\log \\pi_\\theta(a_t|s_t) \\cdot A(s_t, a_t)\\right]$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Implement the A2C agent using the class structure below.\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "class A2CAgent(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, envs)\n",
        "    def get_value(self, x)\n",
        "    def get_action_and_value(self, x, action=None)\n",
        "\n",
        "def train_a2c(env_id, seed, ...)\n",
        "```\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MOaPiZEOk89Q",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "c979d7c0-d7a1-42af-bd3b-a2fe9f5deb55"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "A2C: 6250 gradient updates on 80 samples each\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "# A2C Hyperparameters\n",
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "a2c_gym_id          = \"Hopper-v4\"\n",
        "a2c_learning_rate   = 1e-4\n",
        "a2c_seed            = 1\n",
        "\n",
        "a2c_total_timesteps = 500_000\n",
        "a2c_num_envs        = 4           # Number of parallel workers\n",
        "a2c_num_steps       = 20          # n-step rollout length\n",
        "\n",
        "a2c_gamma           = 0.99\n",
        "a2c_gae_lambda      = 0.95\n",
        "a2c_use_gae         = True\n",
        "\n",
        "a2c_ent_coef        = 0.01\n",
        "a2c_vf_coef         = 0.5\n",
        "a2c_max_grad_norm   = 0.5\n",
        "a2c_norm_adv        = False\n",
        "\n",
        "# Derived\n",
        "a2c_batch_size = a2c_num_envs * a2c_num_steps\n",
        "\n",
        "num_updates = a2c_total_timesteps // a2c_batch_size\n",
        "print(f\"A2C: {num_updates} gradient updates on {a2c_batch_size} samples each\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FhhfG689DJz7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Import all the required libraries\n",
        "class _EnvProxy:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, obs_dim, act_dim):\n",
        "        self.observation_space = type('S', (), {'shape': (obs_dim,)})()\n",
        "        self.action_space      = type('S', (), {'shape': (act_dim,)})()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FKSC1AOcDMbp"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "# A2C Agent Network\n",
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "# This class defines the architecture for an Advantage Actor-Critic (A2C) agent.\n",
        "# A2C has two parts:\n",
        "# 1. A critic that estimates the value of a state (V(s)).\n",
        "# 2. An actor that outputs a probability distribution over actions.\n",
        "# You will create separate networks for the actor and the critic.\n",
        "\n",
        "class A2CAgent(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, envs):\n",
        "        # Initialize the A2C agent.\n",
        "        # Tasks:\n",
        "        # - Determine the dimensions of the observation space.\n",
        "        # - Determine the number of possible actions.\n",
        "        # - Create the critic network (takes state, outputs V(s)).\n",
        "        # - Create the actor network (takes state, outputs action logits).\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Your code goes here\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        obs_dim = envs.observation_space.shape[0]\n",
        "        act_dim = envs.action_space.shape[0]\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.critic = nn.Sequential(\n",
        "            nn.Linear(obs_dim, 256), nn.Tanh(),\n",
        "            nn.Linear(256, 256),    nn.Tanh(),\n",
        "            nn.Linear(256, 1)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        self.actor = nn.Sequential(\n",
        "            nn.Linear(obs_dim, 256), nn.Tanh(),\n",
        "            nn.Linear(256, 256),    nn.Tanh(),\n",
        "            nn.Linear(256, act_dim)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        self.log_std = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(act_dim))\n",
        "\n",
        "    def get_value(self, x):\n",
        "        return self.critic(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def get_value(self, x):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Return the value of a state from the critic network.\"\"\"\n",
        "        # Your code goes here\n",
        "        return self.critic(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def get_action_and_value(self, x, action=None):\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Get an action from the actor and value from the critic.\n",
        "        Tasks:\n",
        "        - Use the actor network to produce logits over actions.\n",
        "        - Convert logits into a probability distribution.\n",
        "        - Sample an action from the distribution (if action is not provided).\n",
        "        - Compute the log probability of the chosen action.\n",
        "        - Compute the entropy of the distribution (helps with exploration).\n",
        "        - Get the value of the state from the critic.\n",
        "\n",
        "        Returns: action, log_prob, entropy, value\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        # Your code goes here\n",
        "        mean    = self.actor(x)\n",
        "        std     = self.log_std.exp().expand_as(mean)\n",
        "        dist    = torch.distributions.Normal(mean, std)\n",
        "\n",
        "        if action is None:\n",
        "            action = dist.sample()\n",
        "\n",
        "        log_prob = dist.log_prob(action).sum(-1)\n",
        "        entropy  = dist.entropy().sum(-1)\n",
        "        value    = self.critic(x)\n",
        "        return action, log_prob, entropy, value"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "m-PuxA7kENGq"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "# A2C Worker + Training Loop (multiprocessing version)\n",
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "# A2C is the SYNCHRONOUS counterpart to A3C:\n",
        "#   - Worker processes each run their own environment and collect rollouts.\n",
        "#   - After each rollout, workers WAIT at a barrier (synchronous).\n",
        "#   - The main process computes GAE and does a SINGLE gradient update.\n",
        "#   - A second barrier signals workers that weights have been updated.\n",
        "# This barrier-based synchronisation is the key difference from A3C.\n",
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "def a2c_worker(worker_id, global_agent,\n",
        "               env_id, seed, num_steps, num_updates,\n",
        "               shared_obs, shared_actions, shared_logprobs,\n",
        "               shared_rewards, shared_dones, shared_values,\n",
        "               shared_next_obs, shared_next_done,\n",
        "               collect_barrier, update_barrier, ep_queue):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    A2C worker process.  Collects rollouts into shared memory buffers,\n",
        "    then waits at a barrier for the main process to do a centralised update.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Unlike A3C, this worker NEVER computes gradients or calls optimizer.step().\n",
        "    The main process owns the gradient update exclusively.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    #Your code goes here\n",
        "    env = gym.make(env_id)\n",
        "    torch.manual_seed(seed + worker_id)\n",
        "\n",
        "    obs, _  = env.reset(seed=seed + worker_id)\n",
        "    done    = False\n",
        "    ep_ret  = 0.0\n",
        "\n",
        "    for update in range(num_updates):\n",
        "        for step in range(num_steps):\n",
        "            obs_t = torch.FloatTensor(obs).unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "\n",
        "            with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "                action, log_prob, _, value = global_agent.get_action_and_value(obs_t)\n",
        "\n",
        "            a   = action.squeeze(0).numpy()\n",
        "            obs_next, r, terminated, truncated, _ = env.step(a)\n",
        "            d   = terminated or truncated\n",
        "\n",
        "            shared_obs      [step, worker_id] = torch.FloatTensor(obs)\n",
        "            shared_actions  [step, worker_id] = action.squeeze(0)\n",
        "            shared_logprobs [step, worker_id] = log_prob.squeeze(0)\n",
        "            shared_rewards  [step, worker_id] = r\n",
        "            shared_dones    [step, worker_id] = float(d)\n",
        "            shared_values   [step, worker_id] = value.squeeze()\n",
        "\n",
        "            ep_ret += r\n",
        "            obs     = obs_next\n",
        "            done    = d\n",
        "\n",
        "            if done:\n",
        "                ep_queue.put((worker_id, ep_ret))\n",
        "                ep_ret = 0.0\n",
        "                obs, _ = env.reset()\n",
        "                done   = False\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Bootstrap next value\n",
        "        obs_t = torch.FloatTensor(obs).unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "            next_val = global_agent.get_value(obs_t).squeeze()\n",
        "        shared_next_obs [worker_id] = torch.FloatTensor(obs)\n",
        "        shared_next_done[worker_id] = float(done)\n",
        "        shared_values   [num_steps, worker_id] = next_val   # one extra slot\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Signal main process that rollout is ready\n",
        "        collect_barrier.wait()\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Wait for main process to finish the gradient update\n",
        "        update_barrier.wait()\n",
        "\n",
        "    env.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "def train_a2c(env_id=a2c_gym_id, seed=a2c_seed, total_timesteps=a2c_total_timesteps,\n",
        "              num_envs=a2c_num_envs, num_steps=a2c_num_steps, lr=a2c_learning_rate,\n",
        "              gamma=a2c_gamma, gae_lambda=a2c_gae_lambda, use_gae=a2c_use_gae,\n",
        "              ent_coef=a2c_ent_coef, vf_coef=a2c_vf_coef,\n",
        "              max_grad_norm=a2c_max_grad_norm, norm_adv=a2c_norm_adv):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    A2C training with torch.multiprocessing.\n",
        "\n",
        "    - num_envs worker processes each run their own environment.\n",
        "    - Workers collect num_steps of experience into shared memory buffers.\n",
        "    - A barrier synchronises: all workers must finish before the update.\n",
        "    - The main process computes GAE advantages and does ONE gradient step.\n",
        "    - A second barrier signals workers that weights have been updated.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    #Your code goes here\n",
        "    mp.set_start_method('fork', force=True)\n",
        "    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Probe env for dims\n",
        "    probe = gym.make(env_id)\n",
        "    obs_dim = probe.observation_space.shape[0]\n",
        "    act_dim = probe.action_space.shape[0]\n",
        "    probe.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "    num_updates = total_timesteps // (num_envs * num_steps)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Shared-memory buffers ──────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "    # values gets num_steps+1 rows so workers can store the bootstrap val\n",
        "    shared_obs      = torch.zeros(num_steps,   num_envs, obs_dim).share_memory_()\n",
        "    shared_actions  = torch.zeros(num_steps,   num_envs, act_dim).share_memory_()\n",
        "    shared_logprobs = torch.zeros(num_steps,   num_envs).share_memory_()\n",
        "    shared_rewards  = torch.zeros(num_steps,   num_envs).share_memory_()\n",
        "    shared_dones    = torch.zeros(num_steps,   num_envs).share_memory_()\n",
        "    shared_values   = torch.zeros(num_steps+1, num_envs).share_memory_()\n",
        "    shared_next_obs = torch.zeros(num_envs,    obs_dim ).share_memory_()\n",
        "    shared_next_done= torch.zeros(num_envs             ).share_memory_()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Barriers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "    collect_barrier = mp.Barrier(num_envs + 1)   # workers + main\n",
        "    update_barrier  = mp.Barrier(num_envs + 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Episode reward queue ───────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "    ep_queue = mp.Queue()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Global agent + optimiser (main process only) ───────────────────\n",
        "    global_agent = A2CAgent(_EnvProxy(obs_dim, act_dim))\n",
        "    global_agent.share_memory()\n",
        "    optimizer = optim.Adam(global_agent.parameters(), lr=lr)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Spawn workers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "    processes = []\n",
        "    for wid in range(num_envs):\n",
        "        p = mp.Process(\n",
        "            target=a2c_worker,\n",
        "            args=(wid, global_agent,\n",
        "                  env_id, seed, num_steps, num_updates,\n",
        "                  shared_obs, shared_actions, shared_logprobs,\n",
        "                  shared_rewards, shared_dones, shared_values,\n",
        "                  shared_next_obs, shared_next_done,\n",
        "                  collect_barrier, update_barrier, ep_queue)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        p.start()\n",
        "        processes.append(p)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Main-process training loop ─────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "    all_rewards = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for update in range(num_updates):\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Wait until all workers have filled the buffers\n",
        "        collect_barrier.wait()\n",
        "\n",
        "        # ── Drain episode rewards that arrived during this rollout ──\n",
        "        while not ep_queue.empty():\n",
        "            try:\n",
        "                _, ep_ret = ep_queue.get_nowait()\n",
        "                all_rewards.append(ep_ret)\n",
        "            except Exception:\n",
        "                break\n",
        "\n",
        "        # ── GAE / n-step advantage ─────────────────────────────────\n",
        "        obs_b      = shared_obs.clone()        # (T, W, obs_dim)\n",
        "        actions_b  = shared_actions.clone()    # (T, W, act_dim)\n",
        "        logprobs_b = shared_logprobs.clone()   # (T, W)\n",
        "        rewards_b  = shared_rewards.clone()    # (T, W)\n",
        "        dones_b    = shared_dones.clone()      # (T, W)\n",
        "        values_b   = shared_values.clone()     # (T+1, W)\n",
        "\n",
        "        if use_gae:\n",
        "            advantages = torch.zeros(num_steps, num_envs)\n",
        "            last_gae   = torch.zeros(num_envs)\n",
        "            for t in reversed(range(num_steps)):\n",
        "                next_val   = values_b[t + 1]\n",
        "                next_done  = dones_b[t]\n",
        "                delta      = (rewards_b[t]\n",
        "                              + gamma * next_val * (1.0 - next_done)\n",
        "                              - values_b[t])\n",
        "                last_gae   = delta + gamma * gae_lambda * (1.0 - next_done) * last_gae\n",
        "                advantages[t] = last_gae\n",
        "            returns = advantages + values_b[:num_steps]\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            returns    = torch.zeros(num_steps, num_envs)\n",
        "            R          = values_b[num_steps]\n",
        "            for t in reversed(range(num_steps)):\n",
        "                R         = rewards_b[t] + gamma * R * (1.0 - dones_b[t])\n",
        "                returns[t] = R\n",
        "            advantages = returns - values_b[:num_steps]\n",
        "\n",
        "        if norm_adv and advantages.numel() > 1:\n",
        "            advantages = (advantages - advantages.mean()) / (advantages.std() + 1e-8)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # ── Flatten over (T, W) ────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "        obs_flat  = obs_b.view(-1, obs_dim)\n",
        "        act_flat  = actions_b.view(-1, act_dim)\n",
        "        ret_flat  = returns.view(-1)\n",
        "        adv_flat  = advantages.view(-1)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # ── Forward pass on main process ───────────────────────────\n",
        "        _, new_logprob, entropy, new_value = global_agent.get_action_and_value(\n",
        "            obs_flat, action=act_flat\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        new_value = new_value.squeeze(-1)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Losses  (slide 7 formulae)\n",
        "        p_loss      = torch.mean(-adv_flat.detach() * new_logprob)\n",
        "        entropy_loss= -torch.mean(entropy)\n",
        "        v_loss      = torch.mean(0.5 * (ret_flat - new_value) ** 2)\n",
        "        total_loss  = p_loss + ent_coef * entropy_loss + vf_coef * v_loss\n",
        "\n",
        "        optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
        "        total_loss.backward()\n",
        "        nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(global_agent.parameters(), max_grad_norm)\n",
        "        optimizer.step()\n",
        "\n",
        "        if (update + 1) % 100 == 0:\n",
        "            recent = np.mean(all_rewards[-40:]) if all_rewards else float('nan')\n",
        "            print(f\"Update {update+1}/{num_updates} | \"\n",
        "                  f\"loss={total_loss.item():.4f} | \"\n",
        "                  f\"recent_ep_ret={recent:.2f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Signal workers that weights are updated\n",
        "        update_barrier.wait()\n",
        "\n",
        "    for p in processes:\n",
        "        p.join()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Drain any remaining episodes\n",
        "    while not ep_queue.empty():\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            _, ep_ret = ep_queue.get_nowait()\n",
        "            all_rewards.append(ep_ret)\n",
        "        except Exception:\n",
        "            break\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nTraining complete. Episodes collected: {len(all_rewards)}\")\n",
        "    return all_rewards"
      ]
    },
