    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PIodew90J6I_"
      },
      "source": [
        "## GAE Questions [$10 \\times 4 = 40$ marks]\n",
        "\n",
        "### Q1. Derive the GAE formula starting from multi-step advantage estimates.\n",
        "The 1-step advantage is just the TD error: delta_t = r_t + gamma*V(s_t+1) - V(s_t). The 2-step advantage looks further ahead combining two rewards before bootstrapping. GAE is an exponentially weighted average of all these k-step estimates where lambda controls how fast the weights decay. This simplifies to a clean recursion: A_t = delta_t + gamma*lambda*A_t+1, which is what gets implemented in practice.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Q2. What happens at the extreme values of λ, and what is a good practical default?\n",
        "At lambda=0 you only use the 1-step TD error which is low variance but high bias since you trust the value function completely. At lambda=1 you recover full Monte Carlo returns which are unbiased but very noisy. A practical default of lambda=0.95 sits close to 1 to keep bias low while still cutting some variance.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Q3. From the GAE lambda sweep experiment, which lambda values perform best and why?\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Values around 0.92 to 0.97 typically perform best because they balance the bias-variance tradeoff well — low enough to reduce noisy Monte Carlo variance but high enough to not over-rely on an inaccurate value function early in training. Very low values like 0.5 tend to underperform because the value network is not accurate enough yet for 1-step estimates to be trustworthy.\n",
        "### Q4. How does GAE relate to TD(λ) from tabular RL?\n",
        "They are essentially the same idea in different settings. TD(lambda) in tabular RL uses eligibility traces to blend n-step returns for value updates, and GAE does the exact same blending but for computing advantage estimates in policy gradient methods. The lambda parameter plays the identical role in both.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DvkqHmA1aGPR"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient (DDPG) [50 marks]\n",
        "<a id=\"ddpg\"></a>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dpxHt985EELc"
      },
      "source": [
        "Implement the Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient (DDPG) agent. We have studied about DDPG agent in the Lecture. Use the function definitions (given below).\n",
        "\n",
        "This class implements the DDPG agent, you are required to implement the various methods of this class\n",
        "as outlined below. Note this class is generic and should work with any permissible Gym environment\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "class DDPG():\n",
        "    def init(self, env, seed, gamma, tau, bufferSize, batch_size, updateFrequency,\n",
        "             policyOptimizerFn, valueOptimizerFn,\n",
        "             policyOptimizerLR,valueOptimizerLR,\n",
        "             MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES,MAX_EVAL_EPISODE,\n",
        "             optimizerFn)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def runDDPG(self)\n",
        "    def trainAgent(self)\n",
        "    def gaussianStrategy(self, net , s , envActionRange , noiseScaleRatio,\n",
        "        explorationMax = True)\n",
        "    def greedyStrategy(self, net , s , envActionRange)\n",
        "    def trainNetworks(self, experiences)\n",
        "    def updateNetworks(self, onlineNet, targetNet, tau)\n",
        "    def evaluateAgent(self)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "j63dzCSlEELc"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class DDPG():\n",
        "    def __init__(self, env, seed, gamma, tau, bufferSize, batch_size, updateFrequency,\n",
        "             policyOptimizerFn, valueOptimizerFn,\n",
        "             policyOptimizerLR,valueOptimizerLR,\n",
        "             MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES,MAX_EVAL_EPISODE,\n",
        "             optimizerFn):\n",
        "        #this DDPG method\n",
        "        # 1. creates and initializes (with seed) the environment, train/eval episodes, gamma, etc.\n",
        "        # 2. creates and intializes all the variables required for book-keeping values via the initBookKeeping method\n",
        "        # 3. creates targetValueNetwork , targetPolicyNetwork\n",
        "        # 4. creates and initializes (with network params) the optimizer function\n",
        "        # 5. creates onlineValueNetwork, onlinePolicyNetwork\n",
        "        # 6. Creates the replayBuffer\n",
        "\n",
        "        #Your code goes in here\n",
        "        self.env               = env\n",
        "        self.seed              = seed\n",
        "        self.gamma             = gamma\n",
        "        self.tau               = tau\n",
        "        self.batch_size        = batch_size\n",
        "        self.updateFrequency   = updateFrequency\n",
        "        self.MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES= MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES\n",
        "        self.MAX_EVAL_EPISODES = MAX_EVAL_EPISODE\n",
        "        self.noiseScaleRatio   = 0.2\n",
        "        self.minSamples        = 1000\n",
        "        self.maxGradNormPolicy = 100.0\n",
        "        self.maxGradNormValue  = 100.0\n",
        "\n",
        "        torch.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "        np.random.seed(seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "        obs_dim     = env.observation_space.shape[0]\n",
        "        act_dim     = env.action_space.shape[0]\n",
        "        action_high = env.action_space.high\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.envActionRange = (env.action_space.low, env.action_space.high)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.onlinePolicyNetwork = PolicyNetwork(obs_dim, act_dim, action_high)\n",
        "        self.targetPolicyNetwork = PolicyNetwork(obs_dim, act_dim, action_high)\n",
        "        self.onlineValueNetwork  = ValueNetwork(obs_dim, act_dim)\n",
        "        self.targetValueNetwork  = ValueNetwork(obs_dim, act_dim)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.updateNetworks(self.onlinePolicyNetwork,\n",
        "                            self.targetPolicyNetwork, tau=1.0)\n",
        "        self.updateNetworks(self.onlineValueNetwork,\n",
        "                            self.targetValueNetwork,  tau=1.0)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.policyOptimizerFn = policyOptimizerFn(\n",
        "            self.onlinePolicyNetwork.parameters(), lr=policyOptimizerLR)\n",
        "        self.valueOptimizerFn  = valueOptimizerFn(\n",
        "            self.onlineValueNetwork.parameters(),  lr=valueOptimizerLR)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.rBuffer = ReplayBuffer(bufferSize, batch_size, seed)\n",
        "        self._initBookKeeping()\n",
        "\n",
        "    def _initBookKeeping(self):\n",
        "        self.trainRewardsList  = []\n",
        "        self.trainTimeList     = []\n",
        "        self.evalRewardsList   = []\n",
        "        self.wallClockTimeList = []\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Q_G5I1RUEELc"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class DDPG(DDPG):\n",
        "    def updateNetworks(self, onlineNet, targetNet, tau):\n",
        "        #this function updates the onlineNetwork with the target network\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        # Your code goes in here\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        for tParam, oParam in zip(targetNet.parameters(),\n",
        "                                  onlineNet.parameters()):\n",
        "            mixedWeights = (1 - tau) * tParam.data + tau * oParam.data\n",
        "            tParam.data.copy_(mixedWeights)\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CJNWp82GEELc"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class DDPG(DDPG):\n",
        "    def gaussianStrategy (self, net , s , envActionRange , noiseScaleRatio ,\n",
        "        explorationMax = True ):\n",
        "        #this function sets the scale of exploration then add the noise of this scale to the greedy action\n",
        "        #and clips it within the range\n",
        "\n",
        "        #Your code here\n",
        "        actionLowVal, actionHighVal = envActionRange\n",
        "        if explorationMax:\n",
        "            scale = actionHighVal\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            scale = noiseScaleRatio * actionHighVal\n",
        "\n",
        "        s_t          = torch.FloatTensor(s).unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "        greedyAction = net(s_t).detach().numpy().squeeze(0)\n",
        "        noise        = np.random.normal(loc=0, scale=scale,\n",
        "                                        size=len(actionHighVal))\n",
        "        action       = greedyAction + noise\n",
        "        action       = np.clip(action, actionLowVal, actionHighVal)\n",
        "        return action\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4xF8v2-cEELd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class DDPG(DDPG):\n",
        "    def greedyStrategy (self, net , s , envActionRange ):\n",
        "        #this function selects the greedy action\n",
        "        #and clips it within the range\n",
        "\n",
        "        #Your code here\n",
        "        actionLowVal, actionHighVal = envActionRange\n",
        "        s_t    = torch.FloatTensor(s).unsqueeze(0)\n",
        "        action = net(s_t).detach().numpy().squeeze(0)\n",
        "        action = np.clip(action, actionLowVal, actionHighVal)\n",
        "        return action\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gf3BIa5OEELd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class DDPG(DDPG):\n",
        "    def runDDPG (self):\n",
        "        #this is the main method, it trains the agent, performs bookkeeping while training and finally evaluates\n",
        "        #the agent and returns the following quantities:\n",
        "        #1. episode wise mean train rewards\n",
        "        #2. epsiode wise mean eval rewards\n",
        "        #2. episode wise trainTime (in seconds): time elapsed during training since the start of the first episode\n",
        "        #3. episode wise wallClockTime (in seconds): actual time elapsed since the start of training,\n",
        "        #                               note this will include time for BookKeeping and evaluation\n",
        "        # Note both trainTime and wallClockTime get accumulated as episodes proceed.\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        #Your code goes in here\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        (trainRewardsList,\n",
        "         trainTimeList,\n",
        "         evalRewardsList,\n",
        "         wallClockTimeList) = self.trainAgent()\n",
        "\n",
        "        finalEvalReward = self.evaluateAgent()\n",
        "\n",
        "        return trainRewardsList, trainTimeList, evalRewardsList, wallClockTimeList, finalEvalReward\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mEUzOqKOEELd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class DDPG(DDPG):\n",
        "    def trainAgent(self):\n",
        "        #this method collects experiences and trains the agent and does BookKeeping while training.\n",
        "        #this calls the trainNetwork() method internally, it also evaluates the agent per episode\n",
        "        #it trains the agent for MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        #Your code goes in here\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        trainRewardsList  = []\n",
        "        trainTimeList     = []\n",
        "        evalRewardsList   = []\n",
        "        wallClockTimeList = []\n",
        "\n",
        "        trainStart = time.time()\n",
        "\n",
        "        for e in range(self.MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES):\n",
        "            epStart  = time.time()\n",
        "            s, _     = self.env.reset(seed=self.seed + e)\n",
        "            done     = False\n",
        "            ep_ret   = 0.0\n",
        "            ep_steps = 0\n",
        "            max_steps = 1000          # <-- step limit per episode\n",
        "\n",
        "            while not done and ep_steps < max_steps:\n",
        "                a = self.gaussianStrategy(\n",
        "                    self.onlinePolicyNetwork, s,\n",
        "                    self.envActionRange, self.noiseScaleRatio,\n",
        "                    explorationMax=(self.rBuffer.length() < self.minSamples)\n",
        "                )\n",
        "                s_next, r, terminated, truncated, _ = self.env.step(a)\n",
        "                done     = terminated or truncated\n",
        "                ep_steps += 1\n",
        "\n",
        "                self.rBuffer.store(s, a, r, s_next, float(done))\n",
        "                ep_ret += r\n",
        "                s       = s_next\n",
        "\n",
        "                if self.rBuffer.length() > self.minSamples:\n",
        "                    experiences = self.rBuffer.sample(self.batch_size)\n",
        "                    self.trainNetwork(experiences)\n",
        "\n",
        "            if e % self.updateFrequency == 0:\n",
        "                self.updateNetworks(self.onlinePolicyNetwork,\n",
        "                                    self.targetPolicyNetwork, self.tau)\n",
        "                self.updateNetworks(self.onlineValueNetwork,\n",
        "                                    self.targetValueNetwork,  self.tau)\n",
        "\n",
        "            trainTime        = time.time() - epStart\n",
        "            wallClock        = time.time() - trainStart\n",
        "            finalEvalRewards = self.evaluateAgent()\n",
        "            evalMean         = np.mean(finalEvalRewards)\n",
        "\n",
        "            trainRewardsList.append(ep_ret)\n",
        "            trainTimeList.append(trainTime)\n",
        "            evalRewardsList.append(evalMean)\n",
        "            wallClockTimeList.append(wallClock)\n",
        "\n",
        "            print(f\"Ep {e+1}/{self.MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES} | \"      # print every episode\n",
        "                  f\"Train: {ep_ret:.1f} | Eval: {evalMean:.1f} | \"\n",
        "                  f\"Wall: {wallClock:.1f}s\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        return trainRewardsList, trainTimeList, evalRewardsList, wallClockTimeList"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "h-F9U8lAEELd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class DDPG(DDPG):\n",
        "    def trainNetwork(self, experiences):\n",
        "        # this method trains the value network epoch number of times and is called by the trainAgent function\n",
        "        # it essentially uses the experiences to calculate target, using the targets it calculates the error, which\n",
        "        # is further used for calulating the loss. It then uses the optimizer over the loss\n",
        "        # to update the params of the network by backpropagating through the network\n",
        "        # this function does not return anything\n",
        "        # you can try out other loss functions other than MSE like Huber loss, MAE, etc.\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        #Your code goes in here\n",
        "        #\n",
        "\n",
        "        ss, acts, rs, sNexts, dones = self.rBuffer.splitExperiences(experiences)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # ── Value network update ──────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "            argmax_a_qs_v = self.targetPolicyNetwork(sNexts)\n",
        "            max_a_qs_v    = self.targetValueNetwork(sNexts, argmax_a_qs_v)\n",
        "            target_qs     = rs + self.gamma * max_a_qs_v * (1 - dones)\n",
        "\n",
        "        qs        = self.onlineValueNetwork(ss, acts)\n",
        "        tdErrors  = target_qs.detach() - qs\n",
        "        valueLoss = torch.mean(0.5 * (tdErrors) ** 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.valueOptimizerFn.zero_grad()\n",
        "        valueLoss.backward()\n",
        "        nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(self.onlineValueNetwork.parameters(),\n",
        "                                 self.maxGradNormValue)\n",
        "        self.valueOptimizerFn.step()\n",
        "\n",
        "        # ── Policy network update ─────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "        argmax_a_qs_p = self.onlinePolicyNetwork(ss)\n",
        "        max_a_qs_p    = self.onlineValueNetwork(ss, argmax_a_qs_p)\n",
        "        policyLoss    = -1.0 * torch.mean(max_a_qs_p)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.policyOptimizerFn.zero_grad()\n",
        "        policyLoss.backward()\n",
        "        nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(self.onlinePolicyNetwork.parameters(),\n",
        "                                 self.maxGradNormPolicy)\n",
        "        self.policyOptimizerFn.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UuGhPN-iEELd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class DDPG(DDPG):\n",
        "    def evaluateAgent(self):\n",
        "        #this function evaluates the agent using the value network, it evaluates agent for MAX_EVAL_EPISODES\n",
        "        #typcially MAX_EVAL_EPISODES = 1\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        #Your code goes in here\n",
        "        #\n",
        "        rewards = []\n",
        "        for e in range(self.MAX_EVAL_EPISODES):\n",
        "            rs   = 0\n",
        "            s, _ = self.env.reset()\n",
        "            for c in count():\n",
        "                a = self.greedyStrategy(self.onlinePolicyNetwork,\n",
        "                                        s, self.envActionRange)\n",
        "                s, r, terminated, truncated, _ = self.env.step(a)\n",
        "                done = terminated or truncated\n",
        "                rs  += r\n",
        "                if done:\n",
        "                    rewards.append(rs)\n",
        "                    break\n",
        "        finalEvalRewardsList = rewards\n",
        "        return finalEvalRewardsList"
      ]
    },
    {
