    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TI-3LH-REELi"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Experiments and Plots [$20 \\times 5=100$ marks]\n",
        "<a id=\"experiments\"></a>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a03JomdeEELi"
      },
      "source": [
        "Run the VPG, REINFORCE on Pendulum and DDPG, TD3, PPO, on Half Cheetah.\n",
        "\n",
        "Plot the following for each of the environment separately. Note based on different hyper-parameters and strategies you use, you can have multiple plots for each of the below.\n",
        "\n",
        "As you are aware from your past experience, single run of the agent over the environment results in plots that have lot of variance and look very noisy. One way to overcome this is to create several different instances of the environment using different seeds and then average out the results across these and plot these. For all the plots below, you this strategy. You need to run 5 different instances of the environment for each agent. As you have seen in the lecture slides, we plot the maximum and minimum values around the mean in the plots, so this gives us the shaded plot with the mean curve in the between. In this assignment, you are required to do the same. Generate plots with envelop between maximum and minimum value\n",
        "For each of the quantity of interest, plot each of the agent within the same plot using different colors for the envelop. Choose colors such that that there is clear contrast between the plots corresponding to different agents.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Plot mean train rewards vs episodes\n",
        "2. Plot mean evaluation rewards vs episodes\n",
        "3. Plot total steps vs episode\n",
        "4. Plot train time vs episode\n",
        "5. Plot wall clock time vs episode\n",
        "6. Based on plots what are your observations about DDPG and TD3, compare the two algorithms.\n",
        "7. What is the advatage of PPO over DDPG or TD3?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "SEEDS  = [42, 123, 7, 2024, 99]\n",
        "COLORS = {'REINFORCE': '#4fc3f7', 'VPG': '#aed581'}\n",
        "def smooth(x, w=10):\n",
        "    if len(x) < w:\n",
        "        return np.array(x, dtype=float)\n",
        "    return np.convolve(x, np.ones(w) / w, mode='valid')\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def plot_envelope(ax, data_list, color, label, smooth_w=10):\n",
        "    min_len = min(len(r) for r in data_list)\n",
        "    mat     = np.array([r[:min_len] for r in data_list], dtype=float)\n",
        "    eps     = np.arange(1, min_len + 1)\n",
        "    mean    = mat.mean(axis=0)\n",
        "    lo      = mat.min(axis=0)\n",
        "    hi      = mat.max(axis=0)\n",
        "    if smooth_w and min_len >= smooth_w:\n",
        "        mean = smooth(mean, smooth_w)\n",
        "        lo   = smooth(lo,   smooth_w)\n",
        "        hi   = smooth(hi,   smooth_w)\n",
        "        eps  = np.arange(smooth_w, min_len + 1)\n",
        "    ax.fill_between(eps, lo, hi, color=color, alpha=0.18)\n",
        "    ax.plot(eps, mean, color=color, linewidth=2.0, alpha=0.92, label=label)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SAocDE90CoCt"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def run_reinforce(seed, env_id='Pendulum-v1', n_train=1000, n_eval=2,\n",
        "                  gamma=0.985, lr=1e-4):\n",
        "    env   = gym.make(env_id)\n",
        "    agent = REINFORCE(\n",
        "        env               = env,\n",
        "        seed              = seed,\n",
        "        gamma             = gamma,\n",
        "        optimizerFn       = torch.optim.Adam,\n",
        "        optimizerLR       = lr,\n",
        "        MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES= n_train,\n",
        "        MAX_EVAL_EPISODES = n_eval,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    agent.trainAgent()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # cumulative steps per episode\n",
        "    total_steps_list = list(np.cumsum(agent.episodeSteps))\n",
        "\n",
        "    return dict(\n",
        "        train_rewards = agent.trainRewards,\n",
        "        eval_rewards  = agent.evalScores,\n",
        "        total_steps   = total_steps_list,\n",
        "        train_times   = agent.trainingTimes,\n",
        "        wallclock     = agent.wallclockElapsed,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_vpg(seed, env_id='Pendulum-v1', n_train=1000, n_eval=2,\n",
        "            gamma=0.98, beta=0.001):\n",
        "    env   = gym.make(env_id)\n",
        "    agent = VPG(\n",
        "        env                        = env,\n",
        "        seed                       = seed,\n",
        "        gamma                      = gamma,\n",
        "        beta                       = beta,\n",
        "        optimizerFn                = torch.optim.Adam,\n",
        "        optimizerLR                = {'policy': 3e-4, 'value': 1e-3},\n",
        "        MAX_TRAIN_EPISODES         = n_train,\n",
        "        MAX_EVAL_EPISODES          = n_eval,\n",
        "        explorationStrategyTrainFn = stochasticExplorationTrain,\n",
        "        explorationStrategyEvalFn  = greedyExplorationEval,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    agent.trainAgent()\n",
        "\n",
        "    total_steps_list = list(np.cumsum(agent.episodeSteps))\n",
        "\n",
        "    return dict(\n",
        "        train_rewards = agent.trainRewards,\n",
        "        eval_rewards  = agent.evalScores,\n",
        "        total_steps   = total_steps_list,\n",
        "        train_times   = agent.trainingTimes,\n",
        "        wallclock     = agent.wallclockElapsed,\n",
        "    )"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Kly-Iv2dC8pA"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "def collect_seeds(run_fn, seeds=SEEDS, **kwargs):\n",
        "    all_results = [run_fn(s, **kwargs) for s in seeds]\n",
        "    keys        = all_results[0].keys()\n",
        "    return {k: [r[k] for r in all_results] for k in keys}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "# Plot\n",
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "def plot_pendulum(reinforce_data, vpg_data):\n",
        "    subplot_cfg = [\n",
        "        ('train_rewards', 'Mean Train Reward',     'Episode', 'Reward'),\n",
        "        ('eval_rewards',  'Mean Eval Reward',       'Episode', 'Reward'),\n",
        "        ('total_steps',   'Total Steps',            'Episode', 'Steps'),\n",
        "        ('train_times',   'Train Time per Episode', 'Episode', 'Seconds'),\n",
        "        ('wallclock',     'Wall-Clock Elapsed',     'Episode', 'Seconds'),\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 5, figsize=(28, 5))\n",
        "    fig.suptitle('Pendulum-v1 — REINFORCE vs VPG  (5 seeds, min/max envelope)',\n",
        "                 fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\n",
        "\n",
        "    agent_results = {'REINFORCE': reinforce_data, 'VPG': vpg_data}\n",
        "\n",
        "    for ax, (key, title, xlabel, ylabel) in zip(axes, subplot_cfg):\n",
        "        for name, data in agent_results.items():\n",
        "            plot_envelope(ax, data[key], COLORS[name], name, smooth_w=10)\n",
        "        ax.set_title(title,   fontsize=11)\n",
        "        ax.set_xlabel(xlabel, fontsize=9)\n",
        "        ax.set_ylabel(ylabel, fontsize=9)\n",
        "        ax.legend(fontsize=9)\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "    plt.savefig('pendulum_comparison.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
        "    plt.show()\n",
        "    print(\"Saved → pendulum_comparison.png\")\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "# Run\n",
        "# ======================================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Running REINFORCE (5 seeds) ...\")\n",
        "reinforce_data = collect_seeds(run_reinforce, seeds=SEEDS,\n",
        "                               env_id='Pendulum-v1', n_train=1000)"
      ],
